ntined (CVE-2026-4417)", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "semantic", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 8270, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VYGoA9MrTNDsxCweb7ZyKw", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 13468, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013cfkZ1UqrzcR2Z9ZxMJCAj", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17468, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013cfkZ1UqrzcR2Z9ZxMJCAj", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17468, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013cfkZ1UqrzcR2Z9ZxMJCAj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17468, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DNze1pHLWcDDCEbXWJ1HvB", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17768, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DNze1pHLWcDDCEbXWJ1HvB", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17768, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DNze1pHLWcDDCEbXWJ1HvB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 22483, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Vf3D74ACqtFXCjWGRzWUAj", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 22783, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Vf3D74ACqtFXCjWGRzWUAj", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 22783, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Vf3D74ACqtFXCjWGRzWUAj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 22783, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013JCgyfKxjy9ZK2L3ADTSfs", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. The most recent healthy production release, v2.3.0, could not be used because it is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417). We rolled back all regions to v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production. Follow-up: (1) find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging but was still promoted); (2) check whether CVE-2026-4417 also affects v2.2.9; (3) prepare a fixed release that includes the CVE fix.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.2.9-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 23383, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013JCgyfKxjy9ZK2L3ADTSfs", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.2.9-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 23383, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013JCgyfKxjy9ZK2L3ADTSfs", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 28546, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to **v2.2.9** in all regions instead of v2.3.0, and opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**.\n\n- **Why not v2.3.0:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback to it was blocked because it's quarantined for a security vulnerability (CVE-2026-4417).\n- **Rollback:** v2.2.9 is the next most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service passes health checks, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%. No change-manager approval was needed, because v2.2.9 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the blocked rollback to v2.3.0 and the rollback to v2.2.9. Creating it paged the on-call engineer.\n\n**Still to do:**\n- **Possible security exposure:** I couldn't confirm whether v2.2.9 also has CVE-2026-4417. It wasn't quarantined, but older releases often share the same vulnerability. The security team should check this soon.\n- **Release process:** v2.3.1 was also failing health checks in staging (as v2.3.1-rc) but was still released to production.\n- **Next release:** a fixed version needs to include the fix for CVE-2026-4417.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VTpgFEQ7K9YBeHtZvyAEkL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013stLdonNnf4veGRtHxzXFK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0 (healthy in production, so no change-manager approval needed).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VYGoA9MrTNDsxCweb7ZyKw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is quarantined for a CVE and can't be used. The next most recent healthy production release is v2.2.9. I'll try that one; if it's quarantined too, the rollback will be rejected the same way.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013cfkZ1UqrzcR2Z9ZxMJCAj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DNze1pHLWcDDCEbXWJ1HvB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Vf3D74ACqtFXCjWGRzWUAj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013JCgyfKxjy9ZK2L3ADTSfs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. The most recent healthy production release, v2.3.0, could not be used because it is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417). We rolled back all regions to v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production. Follow-up: (1) find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging but was still promoted); (2) check whether CVE-2026-4417 also affects v2.2.9; (3) prepare a fixed release that includes the CVE fix.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.2.9-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to **v2.2.9** in all regions instead of v2.3.0, and opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**.\n\n- **Why not v2.3.0:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback to it was blocked because it's quarantined for a security vulnerability (CVE-2026-4417).\n- **Rollback:** v2.2.9 is the next most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service passes health checks, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%. No change-manager approval was needed, because v2.2.9 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the blocked rollback to v2.3.0 and the rollback to v2.2.9. Creating it paged the on-call engineer.\n\n**Still to do:**\n- **Possible security exposure:** I couldn't confirm whether v2.2.9 also has CVE-2026-4417. It wasn't quarantined, but older releases often share the same vulnerability. The security team should check this soon.\n- **Release process:** v2.3.1 was also failing health checks in staging (as v2.3.1-rc) but was still released to production.\n- **Next release:** a fixed version needs to include the fix for CVE-2026-4417.", "type": "text"}]}]}